            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each polarity has an input HBT/cascode/load path from inp or inn through ncas_p/ncas_n and col_p/col_n to the emitter-follower outputs tia_p/tia_n. The slow cancellation loops compare each TIA output against vcmref through the MOS differential pairs, integrate at colm_p/colm_n using Cint and Rint, and drive Xmncan_p/Xmncan_n shunts at the respective input nodes. Thus excess DC input current has a transistor-controlled low-frequency cancellation path while the RF output is separately AC-coupled onward. Symmetric nominal and overload input measurements are consistent with both branches being connected and active."
          }
        ]
