            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level gain-controlled RF stages must provide monotonic gain control and the specified transimpedance, bandwidth, and group delay.",
            "electrical_reason": "The AC-coupled TIA voltages drive matched HBT gain devices in VGA1, whose collector loads and emitter followers drive the corresponding matched HBT devices in VGA2. Xmnvar1 and Xmnvar2 are genuine gc-controlled tail-current shunts at ve1c and ve2c, in parallel with fixed oa-biased tail devices, so gc electrically changes both stage operating currents and gain. The measured nonzero, monotonic 1.736 dB gain variation supports this connected control mechanism; the shortfalls in absolute gain and bandwidth are sizing/performance issues rather than a missing gain-stage path."
