            "electrical_reason": "Although the forward RF path from the TIAs through the two VGAs and buffer to finalp/finaln is connected, the detector ports are connected back to bufinp/bufinn only through Riso_p and Riso_n, each 1.0 megohm. At the detector's 33.5 GHz operating domain, the preamplifier BJT input capacitances present a finite RF load, so these 1 Mohm series elements effectively isolate pkdinp/pkdinn from the receiver RF signal. Consequently the locally valid externally driven detector and the detector-to-agc amplifier cannot form a credible amplitude-responsive feedback loop to Xsw_auto/gc in the complete receiver. The PAM4 forward-path response therefore does not establish the required coherent detector/AGC integration."
